        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Vienna</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 97 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> set up the military camp of Vindobona in the 1st century CE; construction of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legion">legionary</a> camp began around 97 CE, and the name is a borrowing of a Celtic toponym.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">On the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> at the eastern edge of the Vienna Woods, where the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a> meet the Pannonian Basin, in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>; the city is surrounded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-austria">Lower Austria</a>.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Roman camp of Vindobona; the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-babenberg">Babenbergs</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a>; the sieges of 1529 and 1683; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-vienna">Congress of Vienna</a> of 1814 to 1815; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ringstrasse">Ringstrasse</a>; Red Vienna; the music of Haydn, Mozart and Beethoven; the university founded in 1365</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Vienna is the capital and most populous city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> and one of its nine states.</span></div>
